# The SlopOS cargo-fork pin.
#
# `scripts/make_rustc_src.sh` applies the patch below in the rustc source
# tree's `src/tools/cargo`, and `scripts/check_toolchain_pin.sh` fails if any
# line here stops describing what is on disk.
#
# There is no tarball checksum: cargo's sources arrive inside the rustc source
# tarball `toolchain/compiler/PIN` already pins, so the two forks share one
# materialised tree and one stamp. They do not share a PIN, because this patch
# is a PR to rust-lang/cargo and that one is a PR to rust-lang/rust.
#
# What the fork does: puts curl, libgit2, OpenSSL and the pure-Rust crates
# only their code paths reach behind a `network` feature, on by default.
# Without it cargo resolves path, directory and local-registry sources — a
# vendored workspace build — which is what `x86_64-unknown-slopos` can offer
# and all that building SlopOS on SlopOS needs. `rusqlite` stays: SQLite is
# one amalgamated C file and it cross-compiles against slibc.
